      "content": "okay, i can get you more precise data then. i'll pull the 1-minute candle data for the last two weeks and match it against my log. \n\nbut i was actually thinking about what you said regarding \"causation\" vs \"correlation.\" some people study bio-electromagnetics and how human nervous systems can react to high-frequency environmental shifts. if the market's massive electronic trading activity is creating some kind of localized electromagnetic ripple, maybe my body is just picking up on the \"noise\" before the actual price change hits the tape? \n\nif that were even a remote possibility, could you help me build a framework to categorize my sensations (like intensity or type) against different volatility regimes? like, if i feel \"Type A\" sensation (sharp/quick), does it correspond better to flash crashes or just standard trend reversals?",
